| Price versus 200-day simple average ($434.78) | +21.7% above | Long-term trend is up, but price is stretched above its base |
| 50-day exponential average / 200-day exponential average | $496.94 / $455.92 | Price is above both |
| 50-day versus 200-day simple average | $503.91 against $434.78 | Golden cross configuration (50-day well above 200-day) |
| MACD (12, 26) | 12.04, signal line 10.54, histogram +1.5 | Bullish, momentum positive but not accelerating sharply |
| RSI (14) | 71.2 on one site, 62.4 on another | Upper end of neutral to just overbought |
| Distance from 52-week high | -4.5% | Very close to resistance |

*Table 4. Microsoft indicators. Averages and MACD as of 14 October 2026 close.*

The two RSI figures are worth a comment. They were both published for the same date, yet one says 71.2 and the other 62.4. The gap probably comes from how each vendor smooths the calculation and which price series it uses. I would rather show both than choose the one that fits a story. Either way, momentum was warm but not extreme, and the 1.9% fall on 16 October will have cooled it a little.

### 4.3 Patterns I see

- **A V-shaped recovery.** The stock rose about 51% from $349.20 without building a base first. That is a sharp reversal rather than a classic pattern, and it tells me buyers stepped in hard after the sell-off. Fast recoveries leave little support just beneath the price, which is why the 50-day average matters.
- **A defined ceiling at $540 to $555.** The 52-week high of $553.72, the old highs near $555 and the record close of $543.45 all sit in this band. Price has now approached it for what looks like the third time. A ceiling that gets tested repeatedly can end in a breakout or a failure. I cannot tell which from the chart alone.
- **Not a confirmed triple top.** It is tempting to call the repeated highs a triple top, but a double or triple top only counts once price breaks the support between the peaks. Here the trough between the peaks is the $349.20 low, about 34% below the current price. So the pattern is a possibility, not a signal.
- **Trend structure.** Since June the stock has made higher lows, and it has stayed above a rising 50-day average. That is a healthy uptrend by the usual definition.

